+### Stable whole-assembly selection
+
+The user confirmed the revised machine motion is fixed but said the hitbox looked terrible because it moved like one blade rather than encompassing the assembly. Blade and machine-body clicks now resolve to the stationary machine assembly, with an invisible cylindrical raycast volume over the casing and a fixed assembly-wide outline. Wind-turbine blade/tower clicks similarly select a fixed outline covering the whole tower and rotor, using a circular pick area for the blades. Entity selection and controls remain unchanged. Mock-renderer tests use real Three.js geometry and raycasting for the machine proxy, verify blade clicks select the full machine or wind assembly, and check that selection bounds do not change as blades rotate. Visual/device confirmation of the highlight remains necessary; terrain was not evaluated in this feedback.
