+Each installed turbine now has its own top-entry, bottom-exit route; each pump has a side intake connected to the lower outlet and a top outlet connected back to the shared upper penstock. Branch water animation is tied to that unit's actual flow, and pumping reverses its direction; inactive branches contain still water. Continuous, subtle current tint supplements refraction so flow does not depend solely on seeing distorted background; no dotted markers were reintroduced. These are schematic paths and do not change the hydraulic simulation. Pipe geometry compensates for exaggerated vertical terrain scale even on vertical bends. The Penstock camera frames the intake-to-outlet path using viewport aspect and near side-on elevation.
