+# Hydropower Tycoon
+
+A deterministic pumped-storage management simulation with an offline Three.js diorama. **This is a work-in-progress build, not yet accepted against all §14.3 checks.** See `PROGRESS.md` and `reviews/` for known gaps.
+
+## Open and play
+
+Open `hydropower-tycoon.html` directly in a modern browser. No network or server is required. WebGL is needed for the world view; the simulation also runs headlessly. Choose a seed and a Classic or procedural site, then use the operations panel to generate or pump, set flow, and enable or disable automation. Click an owned 3D tile to open its build popover; the Build toolbar button highlights tiles. God mode uses a forecast-based manager with editable rules, reserve, maintenance and investment settings; it is not a guarantee of optimal profit. The toolbar also opens automation, grid, finance, telemetry, and save controls. A manual dispatch turns automation off; damaged dams show a safe-level marker and a repair control. Space pauses, 1–6 selects speed, T advances a turn in turn mode, F1 opens telemetry; Tab moves keyboard focus, C cycles the survey lens, F focuses the selected object, F2 opens debug values, and Escape closes a panel. Saves normally use localStorage; export JSON for a portable backup.
+
+## Rebuild offline
+
+```sh
+node build/bundle.mjs --check
+node build/bundle.mjs
+```
+
+The local, dependency-free bundler packages this repository's static modules and vendored Three.js as two inline scripts. It refuses unsupported external imports and circular dependencies. It does not tree-shake or minify Three.js; see `decisions/bundle.md`.
+
+## Tests
+
+Run `npm test` for the rebuilt bundle, deterministic unit/integration checks, mock-renderer smokes, and both audits (computationally intensive). Run `npm run build` to rebuild only the offline file. The pacing row is report-only and currently outside its income target.
+
+```sh
+node tools/contract-check.mjs
+for f in tests/*.test.mjs; do node "$f"; done
+node tests/selftest-cli.mjs
+node tests/ui-smoke.mjs
+node tests/contrast.test.mjs
+node tests/world-smoke.mjs
+node tests/world-render-smoke.mjs
+node tests/bundle-smoke.mjs
+node tests/audit-worker-smoke.mjs
+```
+
+The full audit is computationally intensive. `SELFTEST_REPORT.md` records the latest results and limitations. The bundle launches the same audit in a Web Worker where supported, exposing `window.__HYDRO_AUDIT__` after it finishes. A browser/headless-GL audit has not been run in this environment.
+
+The designated pacing constant is `CAPEX_SCALE` in `src/config.js`; do not change it without owner approval. The current Test 24 daily income is out of range, and no tuning was performed.
+
+Year-end renewable bonus: 100 times the sum of each eligible site’s year-one renewable capacity factor, using capacity-hours; the decision is recorded in `changes.md`.
