+# Bundle decisions
+
+## Resume
+
+`node build/bundle.mjs` emits `hydropower-tycoon.html`, with vendored Three.js, CSS and application code inlined. `--check` enforces the simulation forbidden-word rule. No packages were fetched or installed. The locked esbuild dependency is absent, so the build uses a small static offline module transformer which rejects unsupported external imports and cycles; it is not an esbuild/tree-shaken/minified build. Bundle size is reported by the build command. `tests/bundle-smoke.mjs` executes the actual inline scripts in a Node VM, confirms Three.js and Game are present, and advances a step. It does not replace a real browser/WebGL test.
+
+The self-test runs in a Blob worker to avoid freezing the UI; the no-Worker path explicitly reports unavailable and is exercised in a fake DOM. Real browser Worker execution is not yet verified. No browser or headless GL executable was found, so the browser audit, console and frame measurements are **NOT RUN**. Full CLI results are in `SELFTEST_REPORT.md`.
