+# Engine decisions
+
+## Resume
+- Implemented `src/sim/engine.js`, `src/game.js`, minimal `src/sim/sites.js`,
+  and `tests/engine.test.mjs` (132 checks). Engine supports the action list,
+  except gameplay-owned actions, which use a handler registry. Browser rendering,
+  gameplay features, and the full audit are the later agents' work.
+- Test 4 (pre-ramped to 1 m³/s, weather disabled): exactly +3600 / −3600 m³,
+  then back to zero, at dt 1, 5, 30 s. Test 15 bought/sold 0.5 / 0.5 MWh at
+  all step sizes (roundoff at most 1.6e-14).
+- Test 12 sim part: 3 days from day 90, all machines maximum, alternating
+  every 6 h, heat-wave and 24-hour storm-rain events injected across day 91;
+  0 nonfinite numbers and reservoir volumes/wear in bounds on every step at all step sizes, with 0 intermediate violations.
+  Battery, reserve and emergency need Gameplay; these are not simulated here.
+- Test 24, report only: estimated mean income $8.99139/day (outside $40–120);
+  indicative §7.4 Tier-2 pair payback 367.948 days. Assumptions: maximum opening
+  in each day's six lowest/highest actual-price hours; 24-hour initial forecast,
+  rated efficiency product for new RTE (0.756) and 0.65 for existing RTE;
+  incremental O&M accounts for capacity and cycle throughput. The methodology
+  should be reviewed; no constants were tuned.
+- Test 25 (10,000 steps): 0.004198 ms/site with one site and 0.007640 ms/site
+  with three; machine-dependent. Climate 61/61, economy 79/79, physics 62/62,
+  contract 10/10. Bundle check cannot load missing esbuild; manual forbidden
+  word check reported zero matches. No dependencies were installed.
+
+## Integration
+- `createEngine(state)` returns `step`, `stepTo`, `dispatch`, `flushActions`,
+  `stateHash`, `getSnapshot`, `getClock`, `registerActionHandler`, and
+  `registerStepHook`. Hooks take one mutable context. `before-plant` receives
+  `{state, site, dt, weather, totals}` and may set `context.Q_env` or unit
+  targets; `after-plant` additionally gets `{plant, water, renewables}` and may
+  add battery powers to `totals`. `before-settlement` receives
+  `{state, price, services}` and may add the just-completed hour's service
+  revenue; `hourly` receives `{state, settlement, price}` after settlement;
+  `daily` receives `{state, endedDay, rain}` after soiling. Aggregate site
+  powers are netted once per step, not separately per site.
+- `site.live` contains the plant result, including `Hf_major`, `Hf_minor`,
+  head, cavitation and NPSH margins, alerts and powers, plus renewable totals
+  and reservoir result `water`; `site.catchmentArea` fixes the drainage area;
+  `site.curtail` holds wind/solar toggles. `site.valleySnow` separately stores
+  land-runoff snow per site and releases it to the lower reservoir over the
+  first warm day; Climate's snowpack handles its own river inflow. No new
+  top-level state keys. `clock.turnRemaining` tracks turn progress.
+- §3.2 explicitly says no river at Classic; ignore climate's river array there.
+  Land-runoff snow retention uses an effective catchment input to the existing
+  reservoir API, leaving lake rain unchanged.
+- Construction jobs are validated on a copy before mutating the real site.
+  §7.1 says purchases cannot take cash below zero, so unused credit requires an
+  explicit loan before purchase despite availableBudget including credit.
+- SET_FLOW uses `{siteId, unitId, targetPct}`; SET_SPEED `{speedIndex}`;
+  PAUSE `{paused}`; SET_MODE `{mode: 'realtime'|'turn'}`; SET_CURTAIL
+  `{kind:'wind'|'solar', curtailed}`. BUILD uses `{kind:'pump'|'turbine'|\
+  'solar'|'wind', tier, parcel?, tile?}`; renewable installations use an owned
+  parcel and a zero-based tile, at most one of each technology per tile.
+  New arrays start clean. REPLACE_PENSTOCK uses `{D, material}` and PLACE_DAM
+  uses `{station}` on a site with terrain. The free H0 dam uses Canyon's existing
+  table builder. The choice of renewable placement payload is an integration
+  convention pending the full Gameplay/UI implementation.
+- `createSite(seed, id)` returns a detached copy of the initial Classic site;
+  Gameplay owns site purchase, terrain assignment, and insertion into state.
+- Determinism: equal seed and action script give equal hashes; a different seed
+  differs; a snapshot restored through `createEngine` gives the same hash and
+  stays identical after a further day. Construction, repair, cleaning, loans,
+  contracts and job completion are exercised through engine actions.
+- TURN_STEP is accepted only in turn mode and queues one full hour per press,
+  including multiple presses before a frame; malformed or unserializable
+  action payloads reject without throwing.
+- `createGame()` wraps the engine with a guarded rAF loop, detached snapshots,
+  and an action log. Errors retain the last good snapshot and pause the engine;
+  a UI error panel/copy button remains the UI owner's responsibility.
+
+## Later integration update
+Gameplay, UI, saving and the 25-row audit are now present. The bundle check works via the offline local bundler, not esbuild. Current sweep includes batteries, reserve offers and emergencies at all three step sizes; see `decisions/gameplay.md` and `SELFTEST_REPORT.md`. The error panel now receives a notification even when the rAF loop catches an exception. This supersedes the early resume notes above.
