+# Gameplay decisions
+
+## Resume
+
+Implemented and integrated battery, reserve and emergency calls, environmental flow, permits and climate drift, automation, sites, quests, alerts and wind damage repair. `tests/gameplay.test.mjs` reports 121 checks. The integrated Test 12 sweep runs 319,680 ticks at dt 1/5/30 with 0 nonfinite values or bounds violations and observes reserve offers and emergencies. A 30-second fixed step crossing the reserve response deadline now evaluates a non-mutating copy at exactly 45 seconds; 0.5 MW succeeds and 0.8 MW fails for the tested Tier-1 setup.
+
+- River snowpack is site-specific as requested; Classic has no river. Valley runoff snow remains separate.
+- Emergency starts uniformly among eligible hours that permit the event to finish that day.
+- Local-only pumping prioritizes preventing imports over normal ramp-down during sudden generation loss.
+- Damaged wind turbines remain offline until an automatic repair can be paid while retaining the player's cash reserve; default reserve is $0.
+- The 15% co-location discount applies to the second technology's equipment, not land.
+- Renewable curtailment accepts both whole-technology toggles and per-unit fractions. Its delivered power also feeds local-only pump control.
+- Test 24 remains report-only and out of range for daily income. Do not tune CONFIG without approval; see `SELFTEST_REPORT.md`.
+
+## Later scoring and placement decisions
+- The starter solar array occupies parcel 1, tile 0, as selected by the user; old saves with an unassigned array are migrated to the first available solar tile.
+- Year-end score uses the user's choice: sum 100 × each site's capacity factor, with capacity-hours accumulated during year 1, each factor clamped to [0, 1], and sites without renewable capacity excluded. The full-year 30-second-step integration test reaches day 366 and records the score.
+- Save metadata includes procedural start bias and optional station. Replay reconstructs both the terrain RNG consumption and chosen station; legacy procedural saves infer starting parameters when possible.
+
+- Automation has an explicit enabled flag. The operations HUD switches it off when a manual dispatch is selected, so manual commands are not silently overridden.
+- Flood cracks use the user-selected 2% qualifying-day chance, top-quarter safe-depth warning, per-day wear, and paid 24-hour repair. Bankruptcy requires an explicit sandbox continuation; emergency credit is issued only once.
