+# World decisions
+
+## Resume
+
+`initWorld(container, Game, onSelect)` renders snapshot-driven Classic/procedural terrain, surface-height water with simple wave motion, configured-profile dams, powerhouse and penstock, tile-positioned solar/wind/battery objects, sun and sky, pooled rain/snow, survey contours, basic naturalistic terrain detail, and adaptive quality. Orbit, pan, zoom, focus, picking and site switching are wired. WebGL failure shows a fallback message. `tests/world-smoke.mjs` covers pure geometry and `tests/world-render-smoke.mjs` constructs actual Three.js geometry and checks shader injection with a mocked renderer. Real browser/WebGL rendering, shader compilation and frame performance are **NOT RUN**.
+
+This is an initial diorama rather than complete §10.3/10.4 coverage. Procedural terrain and the lake footprint are finite-view approximations; shoreline foam, some weather effects, detailed construction visualization, hover/anchored popovers, smooth camera flights and full 3D dam/tile interactions remain. See `reviews/world.md`.
+
+- Dam raise jobs have a translucent progress cap in the scene and a remaining-time status in the operations HUD. This is an indicative visual, not a fully modeled scaffold.
