new file mode 100644
index 0000000..41a04ad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/reviews/ui.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# UI review
+
+1. **Required interactions — §10.2–10.6.** The operations-first HUD exposes manual Generate/Pump/Idle, flow and an automation toggle. Major panels, an initial debug overlay, seed/bias/siting preview, manual dam cost/volume estimates and a 4×4 tile grid exist. Anchored detail popovers for non-tile objects, live NPV for non-renewable investments, some debug fields, remain missing. Budget and target-energy dam solvers are available for Classic and procedural sites. A forecast-based solar/wind NPV quote is available for a selected parcel and tile. Telemetry includes a forecast-price and reserve-requirement overlay, plus rolling 24-hour reservoir and power charts with per-site and aggregate-site scopes. Owner: UI/world.
+2. **Accessibility and responsive verification — §10.1, §14.3.** `tests/contrast.test.mjs` checks semantic text tokens on opaque surfaces; fake-DOM tests check unblocked Tab and Escape from a form, but full browser rendering, translucent compositing, real keyboard traversal, touch targets and viewport behavior remain unverified. Owner: UI.
+3. **Theme detail — §10.1.** `src/style.css` implements palettes but lacks the full prescribed analogue-gauge and paper-grain visual treatment. Naturalistic shader detail is partial. Owner: UI/world.
+
+Verdict: 3 findings.
+
+Owned terrain tiles now open a compact anchored build popover, with an accessible detailed-build fallback if WebGL is unavailable. God mode controls and editable strategy settings are present. These require actual browser and device usability review.
diff --git a/reviews/world.md b/reviews/world.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..eabc35b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/reviews/world.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# World review
+
+1. **Geometry fidelity — §10.3.** `src/world/renderer.js` renders an 8 m heightfield and an approximate procedural lake footprint over the visible region, not the full hypsometric basin; parcel pads are not blended into slopes. Configured class profiles are used for walls. Owner: world.
+2. **Materials/animation — §10.3.** Water has basic sine waves and ice, and the penstock/runner have flow-linked animation, but full shoreline foam, depth-based color, a high-water band, detailed scaffolds and stars are missing. An in-progress dam raise now shows a translucent growing wall cap; its geometry and progress update are exercised only with a mocked renderer. Naturalistic terrain has procedural color/wet-line detail, but the full specified naturalistic material set is incomplete. Owner: world.
+3. **Interaction — §10.3–10.4.** Orbit, zoom, pan, eased focus, picking, selection highlights and basic survey contours exist. Clicking an owned 3D tile opens an anchored build popover; survey choke pins and a direct 3D dam-siting mode remain missing. A form-based dam siting preview and tile grid exist in UI. Owner: world/UI.
+4. **Performance — §10.3.** Landscape changes rebuild the entire mesh. Automatic quality step-down exists, but actual WebGL frame time and shader compilation are unmeasured; no browser/headless GL was available. `tests/world-render-smoke.mjs` uses a mocked renderer. Owner: world.
+
+Verdict: 4 findings.
+
+The downstream channel, procedural upstream river, rock banks and foam are new. Geometry and camera input are covered by mock tests only; visual quality and trackpad/touch direction need real-browser and real-device review.
